			 <note id="GUID-763F86AB-4DDF-43A1-8F43-36E441D306E5"> 
				<ol id="OL_F66AE2DEC84249E69EA9960FBDA812B6"> 
				  <li id="LI_ADD2FFAA286B456D97C3AEA06F1B42F5"><ph>DDP: Dual Die Package,</ph> QDP: Quad Die Package, ODP: Octal Die Package 
				  </li> 
				  <li id="LI_1E5E81252D304141915A06DF8C1B9B4A"> No mixed vendor support within a channel or channel to channel and No mixed memory DRAM down type support (SDP, DDP, QDP) within a channel or channel to channel 
				  </li> 
				  <li id="LI_B2596A4299A94A8B9B476BA04D83FC3D"> Type-4 (T4) 
					 <ph> (2-x-2+) = PCB with 2 build-up layers</ph> Refer to 
					 <b>Stack-Up and PCB Considerations</b> chapter for more details in this document. 
				  </li> 
				  <li id="LI_0057376DE4FA4422A88EDEDCD8B56A7D"> Non-Interleave = The processor is optimized for a side-by-side ball map and placement of the DRAM memory down devices placement. Each memory channel’s signals are grouped together on one side of the processor packages. 
				  </li> 
				  <li id="LI_9AECB128C22541CD9E5D7B59532C01C0">The DRAM Device ODT will be trained by the MRC. 
				  </li> 
				  <li id="LI_9286F2382D16451DAEC23CC069AF5B55">For 
					 , to avoid excessive latency due to ZQ topology, Intel specifies that each ZQ pin must have a unique ZQ resistor. 
				  </li> 
				   
				   
				  <li id="LI_3BA197F05EA846F2A0E711BAD29C78DD"><ph>LPDDR5x</ph> x16 sub-channels can be swizzle within their x64 Memory controller. When swapping channel DQ the CMD/CRTL signals must be swapper as well. 
				  </li> 
				   
				  <li id="LI_ECA4B55EDB654ED7B9EA1DADE7D23F82">To avoid excessive latency due to ZQ topology, Intel specifies that each ZQ pin must have an unique ZQ resistor. 
				  </li> 
				   
				   
				  <li>LP5x 32Gb die density DRAMs supported by NVL and pending eco-system readiness and validation
				  </li>
				   
				</ol> 
			 </note> 
